From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
Subject: [PATCH] bmips: dts: dsl-3580l: fix stale driver name in wlan comments

The comments still call the bcma host driver "bcm6362-wlan-shim", a name
that no longer exists: the driver is host_soc_brcm6362_wlan.c and the DT
compatible is "brcm,bcm6362-wlan-bus-axi".

Comment-only change.

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
---
--- a/target/linux/bmips/dts/bcm6362-dlink-dsl-3580l.dts
+++ b/target/linux/bmips/dts/bcm6362-dlink-dsl-3580l.dts
@@ -134,7 +134,7 @@
 	 * applicano i fixup board-specific via brcm,sprom-fixups.
 	 *
 	 * Il radio integrato non e' su PCIe — sta sul backplane bcma
-	 * AXI/OCP del SoC, esposto dal driver bcm6362-wlan-shim
+	 * AXI/OCP del SoC, esposto dal driver bcma host_soc_brcm6362_wlan
 	 * (vedi nodo &wlan in bcm6362.dtsi). Il match della SPROM
 	 * avviene per phandle (bcma-bus = <&wlan>), non per
 	 * pci-bus/pci-dev. Vedi l'estensione SoC in
@@ -581,7 +581,7 @@
 /*
  * Radio 2.4 GHz integrato del BCM6362 (14e4:435f).
  *
- * Esposto via bcm6362-wlan-shim sul SoC backplane bcma, NON via
+ * Esposto via host_soc_brcm6362_wlan sul backplane bcma del SoC, NON via
  * PCI. La SPROM viene servita da bcm6362-sprom sopra, matchato
  * per phandle (bcma-bus = <&wlan>). Vedi commenti dettagliati
  * sulla bring-up sequence e topologia in bcm6362.dtsi.
